@joshuavial It's a hack, but if I swap out claude instant 100k for gpt 3.5 turbo, it works:

```python
class OpenRouterModel(Model):
    def __init__(self, name):
        if name == 'gpt-4':
            name = 'openai/gpt-4'
        elif name == 'gpt-3.5-turbo':
            # name = 'openai/gpt-3.5-turbo'
            name = 'anthropic/claude-instant-v1-100k'
        elif name == 'gpt-3.5-turbo-16k':
            name = 'openai/gpt-3.5-turbo-16k'
```

I propose that we use claude instant as the default weak model if openrouter is used. Essentially we just turn the above hack into more of a proper solution by setting the defaults from the correct locations in the codebase.

